    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on speed and prime lineup positioning to navigate a challenging set of matchups. Our clear offensive anchor is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), whose matchup against McGreevy provides the highest efficiency score of the day. His projected leadoff role, coupled with a robust 14% platoon edge, makes him a primary target for stolen base production\u2014a critical category given our team\u2019s scarcity strategy. **Junior Caminero** (74.76) follows closely as our most potent threat against a struggling starter; his 19% SP skill advantage against the high-xERA Quantrill positions him as a high-upside play, bolstered further by his slot in the 3-hole. We are also capitalizing on **Trea Turner** (70.26) and **Christian Yelich** (69.63), both of whom benefit from prime leadoff opportunities and favorable dynamic platoon splits that overcome their respective park headwinds.\n\nWhile the top of the order is solidified, we are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Christian Yelich**, **Yordan Alvarez**, and **Casey Schmitt**. **Yordan Alvarez** (53.45) presents a tactical risk today; despite his elite 0.474 xwOBA, his score is depressed by a difficult same-handed matchup against Detmers and a negative platoon shift, meaning he is a start today solely on the strength of his singular talent. On the bench, **Chase Meidroth** (36.08) was the most difficult exclusion. While his historical performance and park factors were competitive, the optimizer ultimately benched him for falling below our 40.0 efficiency floor, favoring the higher-ceiling platoon edges provided by **Colt Keith** (54.35) and **Caleb Durbin** (55.03). We continue to hold **Hyeseong Kim** in the minors and are currently navigating a postponement for **Carson Benge**, but with the current configuration, we are well-positioned to maintain our daily game cap efficiency while hunting for steals and runs.",
